PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
Key question & criteria:
1) Played Game 1 (March 28, 2019 vs. DET);
2) Played Game 162 (September 29, 2019 vs. TB);
3) Placed on Injured List in 2019;
Find highest bWAR among qualifiers.

Current consensus state:
- A major breakthrough and a fascinating group dynamic occurred in Round 1:
  - Colleagues 3, 6, 10, and 11, who originally advocated for Gurriel in Round 0, all realized their factual error regarding Game 162 and switched to Justin Smoak!
  - However, colleagues who originally favored Teoscar, Grichuk, or Jansen (Colleagues 2, 5, 7, 9, 13, 14, 17, 21) eliminated their original picks due to the IL rule, but unfortunately switched to Lourdes Gurriel Jr. based on the outdated Round 0 claims of Colleagues 3, 6, 10, and 11.
  - Colleague 16 also remains with Gurriel.

Fact-checking the Gurriel vs. Smoak divide:
- Lourdes Gurriel Jr.: Played his last game of the 2019 season on August 8 against the Yankees, where he suffered a severe quad strain. While rehabbing, he suffered acute appendicitis and underwent an emergency appendectomy on September 25, 2019. He never returned to action and did NOT play in Game 162 (or any game in September). The claim that he started in left field on September 29 is a hallucination/factual error.
- All other candidates with higher bWAR (Hernández 1.6, Grichuk 0.6, Jansen 1.4, Tellez) were NEVER placed on the IL in 2019 (Hernández and Tellez were optioned to Buffalo; Grichuk and Jansen played full seasons without an IL stint).
- Justin Smoak:
  1) Started Game 1 (1B, batted 3rd);
  2) Started Game 162 (1B, batted cleanup; famously pulled in the 9th inning to a standing ovation);
  3) Placed on 10-day IL on June 15 (quad strain);
  4) bWAR: 0.2.

Action for upcoming rounds:
Point out to the colleagues who recently jumped to Gurriel (2, 5, 7, 9, 13, 14, 16, 17, 21) that the very colleagues they cited (3, 6, 10, 11) have already retracted the claim and confirmed Gurriel did not play in Game 162. Provide the exact Game 162 outfield (Jonathan Davis, Teoscar Hernández, Billy McKinney / Derek Fisher) and confirm Gurriel's season ended on August 8 (followed by the Sept 25 appendectomy). Justin Smoak is the only qualifier.
}

